  "description": "YEGYOB crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R 3 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C114 H116 Dy4 N18 Ni3 O25 6+,6(Cl1 O4 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1A (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1B (Ni) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.378-3.675 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.18-105.84°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [NiII3DyIII4(μ3-OH)6(L1)6(H2O)](ClO4)6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
